depthsOfPowers -- Computes depth of powers of an ideal
******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        L = depthsOfPowers(s,c,I)
        L = depthsOfPowers(s,I)
  * Inputs:
      * s, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, number of powers to compute
      * c, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, (If omitted, it will use c =
        codim I)
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
  * Outputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, The depths of the powers of I
        from 1 to s-c+1.

Description
===========

Computes the depth of $S/I^k$ for $k$ from 1 to $s-c+1$.

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[a,b,c,d,e,f];                       |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = ideal (b*c, b*d, b*e, d*e, a*d*f, e*f);|
|                                                |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                 |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : depthsOfPowers(6,3,I)                      |
|                                                |
|o3 = {3, 1, 1, 1}                               |
|                                                |
|o3 : List                                       |
+------------------------------------------------+

