genericResidual -- Computes generic residual intersections of an ideal
**********************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        K = genericResidual(s,I)
  * Inputs:
      * s, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, 
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 
  * Outputs:
      * K, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, 

Description
===========

returns K = F:J where F is generated by s elements chosend at random from
elements of degrees e_1...e_s in the ideal. If the degrees of the generators of
the ideal are d_1<=...<=d_n, then the e_i = d_(n-s+i) if s<=n, and otherwise
d_1+1...d_n+1, d_n+1...d_n+1.

The call genericArtinNagata calls genericResidual,and produces a list where the
first item is the codepth of (ring I)/K (or -1 if K is not of codim 2), and the
second item is K.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : setRandomSeed 0                                                         |
| -- setting random seed to 0                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = 0                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : S = ZZ/101[a,b,c,d,e]                                                   |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = S                                                                       |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : PolynomialRing                                                          |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I = minors(2, random(S^2, S^{3:-1}))                                    |
|                                                                             |
|               2              2                      2                       |
|o3 = ideal (45a  + 24a*b - 50b  + 10a*c + 48b*c + 45c  - 49a*d - 50b*d -     |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                2                                  2     2              2    |
|     10c*d + 23d  + 3a*e - 7b*e + 8c*e - 4d*e + 16e , 22a  + 45a*b + 17b  +  |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                     2                             2                         |
|     36a*c + b*c + 6c  - 31a*d - 13b*d - 4c*d + 22d  - 27a*e - 30b*e + 44c*e |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                 2     2             2                      2                |
|     + 21d*e + 4e , 24a  + 2a*b + 35b  + 44a*c + 15b*c + 34c  - 41a*d + 18b*d|
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                  2                                      2                   |
|     + 48c*d + 49d  + 41a*e - 15b*e + 16c*e - 13d*e - 32e )                  |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of S                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : assert(genericResidual(5,I) == (ideal vars S)^3)                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : (genericArtinNagata(5,I))_0                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = 0                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

