maxGs -- maximum G_s of a monomial ideal
****************************************

  * Usage: 
        d = maxGs I
  * Inputs:
      * I, a *note monomial ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)MonomialIdeal,, 
  * Outputs:
      * d, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the maximum value of s such
        that I has property G_s (possibly infinity).

Description
===========

Recall that an ideal I has the property G_s if, for every prime P with codim P
<s, the localization I_P is generated by at most codim P elements. For example,
if s = codim I, then I is G_s iff I is generically a complete intersection.

+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x_1,x_2,x_3];                                   |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : I = monomialIdeal(x_1^2,x_1*x_2,x_1*x_3,x_2^2,x_2*x_3);|
|                                                            |
|o2 : MonomialIdeal of R                                     |
+------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : maxGs(I)                                               |
|                                                            |
|o3 = 3                                                      |
+------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

